Ladybird computes the elements that read a size container’s size again
only once a layout gives the container a box. Blink resumes the style
recalc for the descendants of a size container in its StyleEngine’s
UpdateStyleAndLayoutTreeForSizeContainer(), which only the container’s
own BlockNode::Layout() calls — so a container that isn’t laid out never
asks again. WebKit’s TreeResolver::updateStateForQueryContainer() defers
a size container’s descendants, and TreeResolver::resolve() resumes them
once per resolution, after the interleaved layout of the container’s
renderer. And for a container whose frame’s size changed, Gecko’s
nsPresContext::UpdateContainerQueryStylesAndAnchorPosLayout() restyles
its subtree at most once per flush; a container without a frame has
none, so it never restyles one.
